      "range": [
        "spya-e7fdmb",
        "spya-d89xf7"
      ],
      "title": "What (Not) To Do?",
      "gist": "Given deep uncertainty about machine consciousness, we should avoid deliberately creating it while also taking seriously the separate ethical dangers of AI that merely seems conscious.",
      "question": "machine consciousness — how should we act given uncertainty over whether AI is conscious? (a recommendation)",
      "sourceHeading": "What (Not) To Do?"
    },
    "n0133": {
      "id": "n0133",
      "depth": 2,
      "parent": "n0132",
      "children": [
        "n0134",
        "n0135",
        "n0136",
        "n0137"
      ],
      "range": [
        "spya-e7fdmb",
        "spya-zajp75"
      ],
      "title": "Living With Uncertainty",
      "gist": "Whether something is conscious carries real moral weight, but since all theories of consciousness remain uncertain and computational functionalism is a minority view, nobody can be sure what would create or avoid conscious AI."
    },
