      "range": [
        "spya-v98v5u",
        "spya-w8z40d"
      ],
      "title": "Soul Machine",
      "gist": "AI's future is not fixed, and the human capacity to feel truly alive, not disembodied rationality, is what we must protect from being confused with the silicon mirage.",
      "question": "conscious AI — what in ourselves is really at stake as AI advances? (reflection, not a settled answer)",
      "sourceHeading": "Soul Machine"
    },
    "n0155": {
      "id": "n0155",
      "depth": 2,
      "parent": "n0154",
      "children": [
        "n0156",
        "n0157",
        "n0158"
      ],
      "range": [
        "spya-v98v5u",
        "spya-qwvjwn"
      ],
      "title": "Urgency Of Getting This Right",
      "gist": "AI is reshaping society regardless of whether it becomes conscious, and real artificial consciousness would be deeply harmful, so clarity about its prospects is both urgent and a source of hope for human nature."
    },
